>  <Name>
Fluvastatin sodium salt

>  <CAS>
93957-55-2

>  <Formula>
C24H25FNNaO4

>  <MolWt>
433.45 

>  <Bioactivity>
Fluvastatin sodium is an inhibitor of 3-hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl coenzyme A (HMG-CoA) reductase. Fluvastatin is a drug used to treat patients with hypercholesterolaemia. It lowers serum total cholesterol (TC) and low density lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL-C) as well as the serum apolipoprotein B. It also increases high density lipoprotein cholesterol (HDL-C) levels and apolipoprotein A-I levels. In addition to these, fluvastatin has antiatherogenic, antithrombotic and antioxidant effects. 

>  <Pathways>
Metabolism

>  <Target>
HMG-CoA Reductase inhibitor

>  <Receptor>
HMG-CoA Reductase

>  <Reference>
1. Dansette PM, et al. Exp Toxicol Pathol, 2000, 52(2), 145-148.

