>  <Name>
Cyclosporin A

>  <CAS>
59865-13-3

>  <Formula>
C62H111N11O12

>  <MolWt>
1202.64 

>  <Bioactivity>
Cyclosporin A is an immunosuppressive agent, binds to the cyclophilin and then inhibits calcineurin with IC50 of 7 nM, widely used in organ transplantation to prevent rejection.

>  <Pathways>
Others

>  <Target>
Others

>  <Receptor>
Calcineurin;MRP1

>  <Reference>
1. Handschumacher RE, et al. Science, 1984, 226(4674), 544-547.

