>  <Name>
Suramin Sodium Salt

>  <CAS>
129-46-4

>  <Formula>
C51H34N6O23S6

>  <MolWt>
1291.34 

>  <Bioactivity>
Suramin sodium salt is a polysulfonated naphthylurea that inhibits the binding of calmodulin to recognition sites on the ryanodine receptor-1 (IC50 = 4.9 ?M), blocks G protein coupling to GPCRs, and non-selectively antagonizes P2 purinergic receptors (10-100 ?M).

