>  <Name>
Doxazosin mesylate

>  <CAS>
77883-43-3

>  <Formula>
C24H29N5O8S

>  <MolWt>
547.58 

>  <Bioactivity>
Doxazosin Mesylate is a selective, long-lasting antagonist of ?1-adrenergic receptor. Doxazosin Mesylate has been reported to potentiate contraction response to 5-HT in a dose-dependent manner. Doxazosin significantly reduced alcohol drinking and increased water intake in adult male P rats.Studies has indicated that doxazosin could inhibit TNF-? expression in LPS-induced systemic inflammation model as well as reduce the MCP-1 production in LPS-induced pulmonary inflammation model. Additionally, Doxazosin decreased thickness of footpad in the delayed-type hypersensitivity mice model. Doxazosin had been reported to slightly reduce MCP-1 level in the peritoneal cavity of mice induced by thioglycollate. 

