>  <Name>
Methotrexate

>  <CAS>
59-05-2

>  <Formula>
C20H22N8O5.2H2O

>  <MolWt>
454.44 

>  <Bioactivity>
Methotrexate, a folate antagonist, is a potent anti-inflammatory agent when used weekly in low concentrations, the anti-phlogistic action of which is due to increased adenosine release at inflamed sites. Studies have demonstrated that methotrexate polyglutamates are active inhibitors of several enzymatic reactions, including dihydrofolate reductase.

