>  <Name>
Diazoxide

>  <CAS>
364-98-7

>  <Formula>
C8H7ClN2O2S

>  <MolWt>
230.67 

>  <Bioactivity>
A benzothiadiazine derivative that is a peripheral vasodilator used for hypertensive emergencies. It lacks diuretic effect, apparently because it lacks a sulfonamide group. 

>  <Pathways>
Membrane Transporter/Ion Channel; Enzyme

>  <Target>
ATPase inhibitor;Potassium Channel; Carbonic anhydrase inhibitor

>  <Receptor>
Na+, K+-ATPase;Potassium Channel ; CA

