>  <Name>
Disopyramide

>  <CAS>
3737-09-5

>  <Formula>
C21H29N3O

>  <MolWt>
339.47 

>  <Bioactivity>
A class I anti-arrhythmic agent (one that interferes directly with the depolarization of the cardiac membrane and thus serves as a membrane-stabilizing agent) with a depressant action on the heart similar to that of guanidine. It also possesses some anticholinergic and local anesthetic properties. 

>  <Pathways>
Membrane Transporter/Ion Channel; Neuroscience

>  <Target>
Potassium Channel inhibitor;Sodium Channel inhibitor;AChR antagonist

>  <Receptor>
Potassium Channel ;Sodium channel ;Muscarinic AChR

>  <Reference>
1. Sugao M, et al. J Cardiovasc Pharmacol. 2005 Jun;45(6):545-9.

