>  <Bioactivity>
Atropine is an antimuscarinic agent and has shown the pharmacological effects because of binding to muscarinic acetylcholine receptors. Atropine, the orthosteric antagonist, has been reported to compete with [3H]-NMS for all muscarinic subtypes with a potency consistent with the high affinities at the mAChR subtypes

