>  <Name>
Polymyxin B sulfate

>  <CAS>
1405-20-5

>  <Formula>
C56H100N16O17S

>  <MolWt>
1301.56 

>  <Bioactivity>
Polymyxin B sulphate is a mixture of polymyxins B1 and B2, obtained from Bacillus polymyxa strains. They are basic polypeptides of about eight amino acids and have cationic detergent action on cell membranes. Polymyxin B is used for infections with gram-negative organisms, but may be neurotoxic and nephrotoxic.


>  <Pathways>
Microbiology & Virology

>  <Target>
Antibiotic

>  <Receptor>
Others

