>  <Name>
Mitiglinide calcium

>  <CAS>
207844-01-7

>  <Formula>
C38H52CaN2O8

>  <MolWt>
704.91 

>  <Bioactivity>
Mitiglinide is a drug for the treatment of type 2 diabetes. Mitiglinide is thought to stimulate insulin secretion by closing the ATP-sensitive K(+) K(ATP) channels in pancreatic beta-cells. Mitiglinide belongs to the meglitinide class of blood glucose-lowering drugs and is currently co-marketed in Japan by Kissei and Takeda.

