>  <Name>
Chlorophyllin

>  <CAS>
11006-34-1

>  <Formula>
C34H31CUN4NA3O6

>  <MolWt>
724.16 

>  <Bioactivity>
Chlorophyllin refers to any one of a group of closely related water-soluble salts that are semi-synthetic derivatives of chlorophyll, differing in the identity of the cations associated with the anion. Its most common form is a sodium/copper derivative used as a food additive and in alternative medicine. Chlorophyll is present in green leafy vegetables and reaching levels as high as 5.7% in spinach. 

