>  <Name>
Nicardipine HCl

>  <CAS>
54527-84-3

>  <Formula>
C26H30ClN3O6

>  <MolWt>
515.99 

>  <Bioactivity>
A potent calcium channel blockader with marked vasodilator action. It has antihypertensive properties and is effective in the treatment of angina and coronary spasms without showing cardiodepressant effects. It has also been used in the treatment of asthma and enhances the action of specific antineoplastic agents. 

>  <Pathways>
Membrane Transporter/Ion Channel; Neuroscience; GPCR/G Protein

>  <Target>
Calcium Channel;AChR antagonist;Adrenergic Receptor antagonist

>  <Receptor>
Calcium Channel ;Muscarinic AChR;Adrenergic receptor

>  <Reference>
1.Willis AL, et al. Arteriosclerosis, 1985, 5(3), 250-255.

