>  <Name>
Tegafur (FT-207, NSC 148958)

>  <CAS>
17902-23-7

>  <Formula>
C8H9FN2O3

>  <MolWt>
200.17 

>  <Bioactivity>
Ftorafur is a substance being used in the treatment of some types of cancer. It is a combination of tegafur and uracil. The tegafur is taken up by the cancer cells and breaks down into 5-FU, a substance that kills tumor cells. The uracil causes higher amounts of 5-FU to stay inside the cells and kill them. Ftorafur is a type of antimetabolite.

>  <Pathways>
DNA Damage/DNA Repair

>  <Target>
DNA/RNA Synthesis inhibitor

>  <Receptor>
DNA Synthesis

>  <Reference>
1. Sotaro Sadahiro, et al. Cancer Chemotherapy and Pharmacology. 2012, 70 (2): 285-291.

