>  <Name>
Vancomycin HCl

>  <CAS>
1404-93-9

>  <Formula>
C67H77Cl3N8O24

>  <MolWt>
1485.71 

>  <Bioactivity>
Vancomycin hydrochloride (Vancocin) is used in the prophylaxis and treatment of infections caused by Gram-positive bacteria. Vancomycin acts by inhibiting proper cell wall synthesis in Gram-positive bacteria.

>  <Pathways>
Microbiology & Virology

>  <Target>
Antibiotic

>  <Receptor>
