18010-40-7

>  <Formula>
C18H28N2O.HCl

>  <MolWt>
324.89 

>  <Bioactivity>
Bupivacaine HCl binds to the intracellular portion of voltage-gated sodium channels and blocks sodium influx into nerve cells, used for treating cardiac arrhythmias. Bupivacaine Hydrochloride is a local anaesthetic drug belonging to the amino amide group.

