>  <Name>
Dopamine HCl

>  <CAS>
62-31-7

>  <Formula>
C8H12ClNO2

>  <MolWt>
189.64 

>  <Bioactivity>
One of the catecholamine NEUROTRANSMITTERS in the brain. Dopamine hydrochloride is derived from TYROSINE and is the precursor to NOREPINEPHRINE and EPINEPHRINE. Dopamine is a major transmitter in the extrapyramidal system of the brain, and important in regulating movement. A family of receptors (RECEPTORS, DOPAMINE) mediate its action.


>  <Pathways>
Neuroscience

>  <Target>
5-HT receptor antagonist;Dopamine Receptor agonist;Dopamine uptake inhibitor

>  <Receptor>
5-HT receptor ;Dopamine receptor;Sodium-dependent dopamine transporter

