>  <Name>
Norfloxacin

>  <CAS>
70458-96-7

>  <Formula>
C16H18FN3O3

>  <MolWt>
319.34 

>  <Bioactivity>
Norfloxacin(Norxacin) is a broad-spectrum antibiotic that is active against both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria. It functions by inhibiting DNA gyrase, a type II topoisomerase, and topoisomerase IV, enzymes necessary to separate bacterial DNA, thereby inhibiting cell division. This mechanism can also affect mammalian cell replication

>  <Pathways>
DNA Damage/DNA Repair

>  <Target>
Topoisomerase inhibitor; DNA gyrase inhibitor

>  <Receptor>
Topoisomerase II ;DNA gyrase

>  <Reference>
1. Preissner S, et al. Nucleic Acids Res. 2010 Jan;38(Database issue):D237-43.

