82159-09-9

>  <Formula>
C15H13NO3S2

>  <MolWt>
319.39 

>  <Bioactivity>
Epalrestat is an aldose reductase inhibitor. Long-term treatment with epalrestat is well tolerated and can effectively delay the progression of diabetic neuropathy and ameliorate the associated symptoms of the disease, particularly in subjects with good glycemic control and limited microangiopathy.[1]

