>  <Name>
Glycyrrhetinic acid(Enoxolone)

>  <CAS>
1449-05-4

>  <Formula>
C30H46O4

>  <MolWt>
470.68 

>  <Bioactivity>
Enoxolone (INN, BAN; also known as glycyrrhetinic acid) is a pentacyclic triterpenoid derivative of the beta-amyrin type obtained from the hydrolysis of glycyrrhizic acid, which was obtained from the herb liquorice. It is used in flavoring and it masks the bitter taste of drugs like aloe and quinine. It is effective in the treatment of peptic ulcer and also has expectorant (antitussive) properties.

