>  <Name>
Rifaximin

>  <CAS>
80621-81-4

>  <Formula>
C43H51N3O11

>  <MolWt>
785.88 

>  <Bioactivity>
Rifaximin(Xifaxan), an orally administered, semi-synthetic, nonsystemic antibiotic derived from rifamycin SV with antibacterial activity. Rifaximin binds to the beta-subunit of bacterial DNA-dependent RNA polymerase, inhibiting bacterial RNA synthesis and bacterial cell growth. As rifaximin is not well absorbed, its antibacterial activity is largely localized to the gastrointestinal tract. 

>  <Pathways>
DNA Damage/DNA Repair

>  <Target>
DNA/RNA Synthesis inhibitor

>  <Receptor>
DNA/RNA synthesis

>  <Reference>
1. Cheng J, et al. J Pharmacol Exp Ther. 2010 Jul 13. 

