>  <Name>
Pregabalin

>  <CAS>
148553-50-8

>  <Formula>
C8H17NO2

>  <MolWt>
159.23 

>  <Bioactivity>
Pregabalin is an anticonvulsant drug used for neuropathic pain, as an adjunct therapy for partial seizures, and in generalized anxiety disorder. It was designed as a more potent successor to gabapentin. Pregabalin is marketed by Pfizer under the trade name Lyrica. It is considered to have a dependence liability if misused, and is classified as a Schedule V drug in the U.S.  

