>  <Bioactivity>
Benzalkonium chloride is a cationic surface-acting agent belonging to the quaternary ammonium group. It has three main categories of use: as a biocide, a cationic surfactant, and phase transfer agent in the chemical industry. The chemical is a heterogeneous mixture of alkylbenzyldimethylammonium chlorides of various even-numbered alkyl chain lengths. 

