>  <Bioactivity>
Cinnarizine is a drug derivative of piperazine, and characterized as an antihistamine and a calcium channel blocker, it is also known to promote cerebral blood flow, and so is used to treat cerebral apoplexy, post-trauma cerebral symptoms, and cerebral arteriosclerosis.

>  <Pathways>
Membrane Transporter/Ion Channel

>  <Target>
Calcium Channel inhibitor;Histamine Receptor antagonist

>  <Receptor>
Calcium Channel;Histamine H1 receptor

