>  <Name>
Octocrilene

>  <CAS>
6197-30-4

>  <Formula>
C24H27NO2

>  <MolWt>
361.48 

>  <Bioactivity>
Octocrylene is an organic compound used as an ingredient in sunscreens and cosmetics. It is an ester formed by the condensation of a diphenylcyanoacrylate with 2-ethylhexanol. It is a viscous, oily liquid that is clear and colorless. This organic compound can penetrate into the skin where it acts as a photosensitizer. This results in an increased production of free radicals under illumination. 

