>  <Name>
Cetylpyridinium chloride monohydrate

>  <CAS>
6004-24-6

>  <Formula>
C21H38ClN

>  <MolWt>
358.00 

>  <Bioactivity>
Cetylpyridinium chloride (CPC) is a cationic quaternary ammonium compound used in some types of mouthwashes, toothpastes, lozenges, throat sprays, breath sprays, and nasal sprays. It is an antiseptic that kills bacteria and other microorganisms. It has been shown to be effective in preventing dental plaque and reducing gingivitis. It has also been used as an ingredient in certain pesticides. Cetylpyridinium chloride may cause brown stains between the teeth and on the surface of teeth.

