>  <Name>
Busulfan

>  <CAS>
55-98-1

>  <Formula>
C6H14O6S2

>  <MolWt>
246.30 

>  <Bioactivity>
Antineoplastic bifunctional, DNA alkylating agent that causes DNA damage by cross-linking DNA and proteins. Causes double-base lesions mainly at 5'-GA-3' and, to a lesser extent, at 5'-GG-3' sequences. Forms an intrastrand cross-link at the 5'-GA-3' sequence, and to monoalkylation. Induces normal human fibroblast senescence selectively through Erk and p38 pathways

