>  <Name>
Phenacetin

>  <CAS>
62-44-2

>  <Formula>
C10H13NO2

>  <MolWt>
179.22 

>  <Bioactivity>
Phenacetin is a non-opioid analgesic without anti-inflammatory properties. Its analgesic effects are due to its actions on the sensory tracts of the spinal cord. In addition, phenacetin has a depressant action on the heart, where it acts as a negative inotrope. Phenacetin is an antipyretic, acting on the brain to decrease the temperature set point. Phenacetin is also used to treat rheumatoid arthritis (subacute type) and intercostal neuralgia.

