>  <Name>
Panthenol

>  <CAS>
16485-10-2

>  <Formula>
C9H19NO4

>  <MolWt>
205.26 

>  <Bioactivity>
Panthenol (pantothenol) is the alcohol analog of pantothenic acid (vitamin B5), and is thus a provitamin of B5. In organisms it is quickly oxidized to pantothenate. Panthenol is a highly viscous transparent liquid at room temperature, but salts of pantothenic acid (for example sodium pantothenate) are powders (typically white).

